moized elsewhere, or that a prop really is unstable across renders), use them before emitting the finding rather than guessing.\n\nSet the `frontend_category` field on every finding produced by this addendum: `security` for item 2, `a11y` for item 3, `ts` for item 4, `perf` for item 5, and `hooks` for the React-hooks guidance (if provided separately). Item 1 (rendering) and any finding unrelated to this addendum leave `frontend_category` empty.\n","truncated":false,"exit_code":0,"wall_time_seconds":0}},"isError":false,"durationMs":24}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"p3b8muOVu79OyrQc4PSt4YlN6sgiL2dG","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cat /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-15-prompts/internal/prompts/templates/finder_react_hooks_addendum.tmpl"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nReact-hooks-specific guidance for this diff (highest-yield dimension — these are usually genuine correctness bugs, not style nits):\n\n- Stale closures: missing or wrong dependencies in `useEffect`/`useCallback`/`useMemo` that cause the hook to close over a stale value.\n- Missing effect cleanup: timers, subscriptions, event listeners, or other resources started in `useEffect` with no cleanup function — these leak.\n- `setState(x + 1)` instead of a functional update (`setState(x => x + 1)`) inside an async callback or interval/timeout closure, where the closed-over value is stale by the time it runs.\n- Conditional or looped hook calls — hooks called inside an `if`, loop, or after an early return, violating the rules of hooks.\n- An effect that should be an event handler: side effects gated on a state change that only ever happens in response to a specific user action, when handling it directly in the handler would avoid the extra render and the dependency-tracking complexity.\n\nUse `read_file`/`grep_repo` to confirm a dependency really is unstable across renders (e.g. it's not already memoized elsewhere) before flagging a missing-dependency finding.\n\nSet `frontend_category` to `hooks` on every finding produced by this addendum.\n"}],"details":{}}}
